# The save survives being written down and read back.
#
# The suite runs ONE launch per script, so a real save-quit-relaunch-load test cannot be expressed
# here — see cli/system/save_resume.cli for what the file layer can be asserted on in one process,
# and tests/save_reload.sh for the genuine two-launch check.
#
# What this covers instead is the failure that actually bites: a field added to a party type and
# forgotten in PartyState's DTO, which resets silently on every load. `save roundtrip` captures the
# live run, serialises it, rebuilds a whole protagonist from the text, re-captures, and compares —
# and separately asserts the reference topology, which a text comparison is blind to (two modus
# mentis objects where the live graph had one serialise identically while consolidate/archive/reject
# silently stop working).
#
# This script's job is BREADTH of state, not depth of play: the flags stack a party that exercises
# every branch of Capture/Rebuild at once — a companion (the only member that is not a Protagonist),
# granted items (including a container, so the recursive contents branch runs), and granted modi
# mentis above level 1 (so level and experience are not all at their defaults, where a dropped field
# would still compare equal).
#
# Post-action state is covered for free by appending `save roundtrip` to the verb scripts, which
# already reach it by a route that is maintained. Re-deriving a narration sequence here would be a
# second copy of that route, and it stalled on exactly the preview-box step CLAUDE.md warns about.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --fill-party --grant-item axe,sack --grant-mm woodcraft,scrutiny:3 --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --period noon --save-path .tmp-cli-save/roundtrip.json

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 45

# A fresh party: organ scores, four humor queues of 49, five memory modules, granted items and modi
# mentis, and a companion.
inspect save
expect-state save companions=1
expect-state save seed=42
save roundtrip

# Inside a location: instance state exists and the protagonist has a CurrentLocationId.
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 45

# Drain the opening observation's preview box FIRST. The footer only becomes LEAVE once it is gone,
# so pressing the button before this sits on the preview until the wait times out — the stall
# cli/system/routine_movement_only.cli documents at its own exit.
advance 12 90
save roundtrip

# Back out at the world map, where the autosave fires and location memory has been recorded.
click button
wait mode WorldView 45
save roundtrip

# The visit is remembered, and the autosave on the way out wrote it.
expect-state save locations=1
expect-state savefile locations=1

quit
